---
// Terms of Use (owner, Oct 1, 2026): short, plain terms for this website,
// replacing the old WordPress "Terms & Conditions" (which was a privacy
// notice). The address is kept so old links keep working. Privacy belongs in
// /privacy-policy only; this page links to it.
// Counsel to review before launch.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Banner from '../components/Banner.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="The terms that apply when you use the Technical Source website.">
  <Banner eyebrow="Legal" compact>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="banner-sub">Last updated October 2026</p>
  </Banner>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose legal">
      <h2>Using This Site</h2>
      <p>This website is run by Technical Source, LLC, a North Carolina company. By using it, you agree to these terms. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the site. These terms cover this website only; work we do with clients and consultants is covered by our separate written agreements. How we handle personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Our Content</h2>
      <p>The text, graphics, logos and other content on this site belong to Technical Source or are used with permission. You’re welcome to view the site for your own personal or business use and to share links to our pages. Please don’t copy, scrape, republish or reuse our content without our written permission. Our name and logo are ours: please don’t use them in a way that suggests we endorse you or your business. Stock photos are used under their own licenses, listed on our <a href="/photo-credits">Photo Credits</a> page.</p>

      <h2>Information Is General</h2>
      <p>The information on this site is general. We work to keep it accurate, but we can’t promise it’s complete or current, and it isn’t professional, legal, financial or technical advice for your situation.</p>

      <h2>Job Postings</h2>
      <p>Job postings describe openings we’re working on. They are not an offer of employment or a contract. Positions may change, be filled or close at any time, and pay and other details in a posting can change. Applying doesn’t guarantee an interview or a job. Technical Source is an equal opportunity employer.</p>

      <h2>Our Chat Assistant</h2>
      <p>Our chat assistant’s answers are generated automatically by artificial intelligence. They may be wrong or incomplete, and they are not commitments, offers or advice from Technical Source. Please don’t share sensitive personal information in the chat, such as Social Security numbers or financial or health details. Where a question needs one, a person from our team follows up. Chat conversations are handled as described in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>What You Send Us</h2>
      <p>When you send us a form, a resume or a referral, you confirm that the information is accurate and that you’re allowed to share it. For a referral, that means the person you refer knows you’re passing their details to us. We use what you send as our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> describes.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>Please don’t:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the site for anything unlawful;</li>
        <li>try to harm, overload or break into the site or the systems behind it;</li>
        <li>scrape or collect content from the site with automated tools;</li>
        <li>send us false information;</li>
        <li>pretend to be someone else.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may block access for anyone who doesn’t follow these terms.</p>

      <h2>Links to Other Sites</h2>
      <p>Our site links to other websites, such as LinkedIn and the original articles behind our Insights. We don’t control those sites and aren’t responsible for their content or practices.</p>

      <h2>No Warranties</h2>
      <p>The site is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind. We don’t promise it will always be available or free of errors.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the extent the law allows, Technical Source is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential losses arising from your use of this site or your reliance on its content. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have that the law doesn’t allow us to limit.</p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina. Any dispute about them or this site will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Wake County, North Carolina.</p>

      <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we post the new version here with a new date. Using the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
